# Files whose exact bytes are recorded as SHA-256 (draws manifest, fitting-data identity,
# fit provenance, code identity). Git must never convert their line endings on checkout or
# commit: with core.autocrlf=true on Windows the converted draws failed their manifest
# check (review 6.1, 2026-11-09). Several data files are stored with CRLF on purpose, so
# "-text" (keep the stored bytes) is used rather than "eol=lf".
draws/** -text
data/** -text
fit/stan/*.stan -text
R/*.R -text
docs/development/2026_10_21_v3/double_entry/** -text
